        "answer": {
          "short": "B",
          "worked": "Choose the edges of weights $22,29,30,36,40,42$, avoiding cycles. Their total is $199$ km, leaving four connected components.\n\nFor $x=50$, use the $x$ edge to join the two main components, then the $52$ km edge from the central vertex to the upper-right vertex. Connect the rightmost town using the smaller of $y$ and $60$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}L&=199+50+52+\\min(y,60)\\\\&=301+\\min(y,60).\\end{aligned}$$\nThus A gives $356$ km and B gives $361$ km.\n\nFor $x=55$, the two $52$ km edges connect the main components and the upper-right vertex more cheaply than using $x$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}L&=199+52+52+\\min(y,60)\\\\&=303+\\min(y,60).\\end{aligned}$$\nThus C gives $358$ km and D gives $363$ km.\n\nCorrect answer: B.",
